|{{tl|peh}} or {{tl|page end hyphen}}
| First page: <code>sister-in{{tl|peh}}</code><br/>
Next page: <code>law</code>
| ''sister-in-law.'' Use when a hyphen at the end of a page should be ''kept'' when transcluded, because the hyphen is part of the word. See [[H:HYPHEN]].
|-<!--2ND ROW-->
|{{tl|hws}} and {{tl|hwe}},
or (on new pages) nothing
| First page: <code>{{tlp|hws|sis|sister}}</code>, or just <code>sis-</code><br/>
Next page: <code>{{tlp|hwe|ter|sister}}</code>, or just <code>ter</code>
| ''sister.'' Use when a hyphen at the end of a page should ''not'' be kept when transcluded, because the hyphen is not part of the word. See [[H:HYPHEN]].
|-<!--3RD ROW-->
| {{tl|nop}}
| {{tl|nop}} on its own line
|Paragraph break. Use when the end of a page is also the end of a paragraph.
|}

